== 6. What 37b needs from this ================================= 
  1. the matrix file name, its delimiter, and which axis is genes 
  2. the EXACT feature spelling for RASSF9 (symbol or Ensembl, 
     versioned or not) -- or confirmation that it is absent, which 
     would itself be a finding about the reference annotation rather 
     than about melanocyte biology 
  3. the value scale, so counts are not treated as TPM 
  4. the cell-type column and the exact melanocyte label string 
  5. whether donor, age/stage and anatomical site are present, since 
     those decide whether any stratified test is possible at all 
 
  NOTE: if RASSF9 is absent as a feature, that is NOT evidence it is 
  unexpressed. It would mean the processed matrix was filtered, and 
  the test would have to move to the raw data. 37b will distinguish 
  these two cases rather than reporting either as absence. 
